---
title: Beef with Bean Sprouts (Ngao Yuk Chau Nga Choi 牛肉炒豆芽)
description: Classic quick-fire stir-fry with velveted beef and crunchy bean sprouts. A restaurant-style dish ready in minutes.
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 10 minutes
servings: 3
tags:
  - beef
  - stir-fry
  - quick
  - chinese
source: https://thewoksoflife.com/beef-bean-sprouts
cuisine: Chinese
course: Main
---

== Velvet the Beef ==
-- Velveting with baking soda and cornstarch keeps the beef incredibly tender
Marinate the @sliced flank steak{450%g} with @light soy sauce{15%g}, @Shaoxing wine{15%g}, @cornstarch{8%g}, @baking soda{1%g}, and @neutral oil{14%g}. Set aside.

== Prepare the Sauce ==
Mix the stir-fry sauce: @oyster sauce{35%g}, @light soy sauce{15%g}, @sugar{4%g}, @broth{60%g}, and @cornstarch{3%g}.

== Sear the Beef ==
Heat @neutral oil{28%g} in a #wok{} over high heat until smoking. Add the marinated beef in a single layer. Sear for ~{1%minute} undisturbed, then stir-fry for ~{1%minute} until just browned. Remove the beef and set aside.

== Stir-fry ==
-- Bean sprouts must be patted completely dry to prevent boiling instead of frying
In the same wok, add a touch more oil if dry. Add the @minced garlic{2%cloves} and @minced ginger{5%g}; cook for ~{15%seconds} until fragrant.
Pour in the mixed sauce and let it bubble and thicken for ~{30%seconds}.
Return the beef to the wok along with the @fresh bean sprouts{250%g} (patted completely dry). Toss everything rapidly over high heat for exactly ~{60%seconds}. Serve immediately.
